 "result": "I built fibmod.py. It uses fast doubling, and it reduces n modulo the Pisano period 2*(M+1) first. That period holds because 1e9+7 is 2 mod 5, so 5 is a non-residue. Checks: fib(10)=55. fib(1000)=517691607, which matches an independent iterative loop. fib(10**18)=209783453. The assay runs 20000 calls at n near 10**18. It scored 3.77 at baseline, and the Pisano change gave about +105%. I did not check fib(10**18) against a second method, but the period reduction agrees with the iterative loop at n=1000. I did not test any other large n.",
